{# ===========================================================================
   Component: menu-concept

   The shared body of the menu module, ported from the approved concepts in
   _reference/menu-concepts/. A2 is what the location pages render as of
   2026-09-14; B2 and B1 remain for the internal review routes.

   EXPECTS
     variant       "a2" (photo per dish) | "b2" (three columns) | "b1" (two
                   columns + peek)
     showPrices    boolean
     mcLoc         location id, defaults to east-village
     mcChrome      true for the standalone review routes (masthead + h1 +
                   legend + fine print), false when the module sits inside a
                   location page that already has its own h1 and footer
     mcPhotoScope  "location" (default) | "site". See the note below.

   The reference's structure, reproduced: a coloured spine block down the left
   of each section with rotated display type, no full-width bar; a cut rule
   with a brand mark between sections; a 92px square photograph beside every
   dish with the name and price in the brush face on one line and the
   description beneath; ghosted brand art bottom right of each band; dietary
   glyphs inline after the name; the legend and fine print at the foot.

   WHAT THE A2 PORT DOES NOT CARRY, all reported rather than quietly dropped.
   The mockup has a fourth band (Rice) that menu.json has no section for; an
   "Extra ramen toppings" block that is a price list end to end, with no data
   behind it; prices on every card, which /menu/ pulled on 2026-09-10; and a
   photo lightbox with a mobile detail sheet, which is interaction rather than
   layout and was not in the brief. Building any of them would mean
   transcribing rows out of the reference HTML.

   DATA. Rows come from menu.json through `dishesFor`, scoped to the location.
   Nothing is transcribed from the reference HTML.
   =========================================================================== #}
{%- set mcLocId = mcLoc | default("east-village") %}
{%- set mcRoom = (locations.items | where("id", mcLocId)) | first %}
{%- set mcChromeOn = mcChrome | default(false) %}
{#-
  WHERE A2's DISH PHOTOGRAPHS COME FROM, and it is not the same answer on
  every route.

  "location" (a published location page) asks _data/dishPhotos.js for the
  photograph of that dish, preferring a frame shot in that room when one exists
  and falling back to the house frame.

  IT USED TO BE SCOPED BY FILENAME and that is why this variant sat unshipped:
  photos.json's `_rule` said a photo reaches a location page only if its
  filename names that location, every dish photograph is named for Convoy or
  Kihei, and so five of seven rooms rendered placeholder tiles on every card.
  The rule was written for rooms and was wrong for food. Amended 2026-09-15;
  see `_rule` and `_ruleHistory` in photos.json. A bowl of Tajima Red is the
  same bowl in every room.

  "site" (the internal review routes) reads menu.json's `image`, the site-wide
  field that /menu/ and the homepage already use. Those routes are noindex
  internal reviews of a DESIGN against the reference's own room, not pages that
  claim a photograph was taken anywhere, and the footer says in one line that
  the dish photography was shot at Convoy. Nothing here reaches the public site
  through that path.
-#}
{%- set mcPhotos = mcPhotoScope | default("location") %}
{#-
  THE SECTION LIST IS DATA NOW, 2026-09-15. It was three keys hardcoded here,
  which was true while menu.json held fourteen dishes and three sections. The
  file is the full catalog since Connor's dish sheet landed and carries eight:
  izakaya, ramen, rice, sushi, monthly special, dessert, kids, combo.

  A room renders only the sections it has dishes in, so the count varies and
  that is the point. Mercury renders seven, Plaza Bonita three, the other four
  San Diego rooms four, Maui two. The old hardcoded three would have hidden
  thirty-nine of Mercury's forty-seven dishes.

  Order and labels come from menuConcepts.json. The spine tones are checked
  against every room's real band sequence by a guard in eleventy.config.js that
  fails the build if two touching bands share a tone.
-#}
{#-
  WHERE THE ROWS COME FROM, and it is two answers now.

  `mcSections` is passed in by components/location-menu.njk and holds that
  room's own Toast catalog, already excluded, joined and ordered by
  _data/roomMenus.js. A published location page carries ITS ROOM'S FULL MENU
  and that is the whole point of the rebuild.

  With no `mcSections` the module falls back to menu.json filtered by
  location, which is what the internal review routes at /internal/ still do.
  They review a DESIGN against the reference's own room, so they should keep
  reading the reference's own data.

  Either way the component below sees one shape: a list of bands, each with a
  key, a label and rows carrying name, description, dietary and photo.
-#}
{%- set mcBands = [] %}
{%- if mcSections %}
  {%- set mcBands = mcSections %}
{%- else %}
  {%- for key in menuConcepts.sectionOrder %}
    {%- set legacyRows = menu.items | dishesFor(mcLocId, key) %}
    {%- if legacyRows | length %}
      {%- set mcBands = (mcBands.push({ key: key, label: menuConcepts.sectionLabels[key], items: legacyRows }), mcBands) %}
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if mcChromeOn %}
<div class="mc__mast">
  <p class="mc__kicker">{{ mcRoom.address.street }}, {{ mcRoom.address.locality }}</p>
  <h1 class="mc__title">What comes out of <em>{{ mcRoom.name }}.</em></h1>
  <p class="mc__note">This room's own list. Walk in, no reservations.</p>
</div>
{%- else %}
{#- Inside a location page the page already owns the h1, so the module leads
    with an h2 and the section names drop to h3.

    THE HEADING SAYS WHAT THE LIST IS, 2026-09-16. It read "What comes out of
    [Room]", which is a voice line rather than a label, and a first-time
    reader could not tell from it whether they were looking at the full menu,
    a selection, or that room's specialities. It is the full menu now, so it
    says so.

    IT DOES NOT PROMISE COMPLETENESS, because it cannot: these rows are a
    2026-08-04 snapshot of the room's Toast catalog and Toast is where the
    list actually lives. The note says both things in one sentence rather
    than hedging the heading into meaning nothing. -#}
<header class="mc__head">
  <h2 class="mc__title mc__title--inline">The menu at <em>{{ mcRoom.name }}.</em></h2>
  <p class="mc__note mc__note--inline">
    Every room runs its own menu, and this is {{ mcRoom.name }}'s. Toast carries the live
    list and anything added since.
  </p>
</header>
{%- endif %}

{%- for section in mcBands %}
{%- set rows = section.items %}
{%- if rows | length %}
{%- set tone = menuConcepts.barTones[section.key] %}
{%- set ornament = menuConcepts.ornaments[section.key] %}
{%- set cut = menuConcepts.cuts[section.key] %}
{%- set featured = rows | firstWithReviewedPhoto %}

{%- if not loop.first %}
{#- The cut. A brand mark sitting in the spine column, then a hairline across
    the rest. Decorative divider, so it is hidden from assistive technology.

    THE RULE ALWAYS DRAWS, THE MARK ONLY SOMETIMES. Four of the eight sections
    have no matching sprite icon (sushi, monthly special, kids, combo: the
    sprite is twelve marks and every one is a ramen component, an izakaya dish
    or the wordmark). DESIGN_SYSTEM.md says where no icon matches, use none, so
    those get no mark. They still get the rule, because a band with no cut mark
    is not a band with no divider: without it Mercury's seven sections would run
    into each other. The mark column keeps its width either way so the rules all
    start at the same x. -#}
<div class="mc-cut" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="mc-cut__mark">{% if cut %}<svg><use href="#i-{{ cut }}"></use></svg>{% endif %}</span>
  <span class="mc-cut__rule"></span>
</div>
{%- endif %}

{#- data-mc-band is read by src/js/menu-lightbox.js: it marks a band as one
    navigable group and carries the label the dialog shows. Stepping is scoped
    to the section a reader tapped in, so arrows and swipe do not walk out of
    Ramen and into Dessert. -#}
<section class="mc-band mc-band--{{ tone }}" data-mc-band="{{ section.label }}" aria-labelledby="mc-{{ section.key }}{% if not mcChromeOn %}-{{ mcLocId }}{% endif %}">
  {#- The mobile section header. The spine is a vertical block and cannot
      survive a 360px column, so below 47.5rem it is hidden and this sticky
      tone bar takes over, which is exactly what the reference does. Hidden
      from assistive technology on both sides of that swap because the real
      h2 is in the row below and would otherwise be announced twice. -#}
  <div class="mc-band__bar" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.label }}</div>

  <div class="mc-band__row">
    {#- The spine. Rotated display type on the tone block, the device the
        reference is built on. It repeats the heading beside it, so the visible
        text is aria-hidden and the real h2 is visually hidden next to it. -#}
    <div class="mc-band__spine" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.label }}</div>
    {%- if mcChromeOn %}
    <h2 class="u-visually-hidden" id="mc-{{ section.key }}">{{ section.label }}</h2>
    {%- else %}
    <h3 class="u-visually-hidden" id="mc-{{ section.key }}-{{ mcLocId }}">{{ section.label }}</h3>
    {%- endif %}

    <div class="mc-band__body">
      {%- if ornament %}
      <div class="mc-band__art" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#i-{{ ornament }}"></use></svg></div>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if section.key == "ramen" %}
      {#- The confirmed slogan from site.json. The reference prints "Fresh
          noodles crafted daily", which is not the locked string. -#}
      <p class="mc-band__blurb">{{ site.slogan.before }}{{ site.slogan.emphasis }}</p>
      {%- endif %}

      <div class="mc-split{% if variant == 'b1' and featured %} mc-split--peek{% endif %}">
        {%- if variant == "a2" %}
        {#- A2: a square thumbnail per dish beside the name, price and
            description, three across, exactly as the reference does it.

            A DISH WITH NO PHOTOGRAPH GETS THE REFERENCE'S OWN EMPTY STATE: a
            tinted tile the same 92px square as a photograph, carrying a
            ghosted brand mark. That keeps the text column starting at the same
            x down the whole grid, which a text-only card would not, and it is
            what the mockup specifies for its own three photo-less dishes. No
            broken image, no filename, no grey rectangle.

            It is aria-hidden and carries no alt, because it says nothing: the
            dish's name and description are right beside it. -#}
        <ul class="mc-plates">
          {%- for dish in rows %}
          {#- roomMenus resolves the photograph when it builds the row, because
              it also has to count coverage. A menu.json row from the legacy
              branch still needs the lookup. -#}
          {%- set shot = dish.photo if dish.photo else (dishPhotos.photoFor(dish.id, mcLocId) if mcPhotos == "location" else null) %}
          {#- BARE ROWS: no photo, no placeholder tile, no description. Toast
              carries both French Fries (all six rooms) and Mercury's Sushi
              Rice with description: null, and neither is a row in Connor's
              sheet or on the July printed menus, checked directly against
              both. There is nothing to show beside the name, so the ghosted
              placeholder tile that stands in for a missing PHOTO stops being
              the right device: pairing it with a missing description too
              left a 92px square of dead air beside one line of text. A bare
              row drops the tile and lets .mc-plate--bare collapse to a
              single column, so the card is short on purpose rather than
              short by accident. -#}
          {%- set bare = not shot and not (mcPhotos == "site" and dish.image) and not dish.description %}
          <li class="mc-plate{% if bare %} mc-plate--bare{% endif %}">
            {%- if shot %}
            <span class="mc-shot">
              {#- data-full is the original, and it is an ATTRIBUTE rather than
                  a src so the browser never fetches it until the lightbox
                  asks. The tile itself is the 184px derivative. -#}
              <img src="{{ shot.thumb | default(shot.src) }}" alt="{{ shot.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                width="{{ shot.thumbWidth | default(shot.width) }}" height="{{ shot.thumbHeight | default(shot.height) }}"
                data-full="{{ shot.src }}" data-full-w="{{ shot.width }}" data-full-h="{{ shot.height }}">
            </span>
            {%- elif mcPhotos == "site" and dish.image %}
            <span class="mc-shot">
              <img src="{{ dish.image }}" alt="{{ dish.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="{{ dish.imageWidth }}" height="{{ dish.imageHeight }}">
            </span>
            {%- elif not bare %}
            {#- The placeholder falls back to the ramen bowl when its own
                section has no ornament. Four of the eight sections have no
                matching sprite icon, and without a fallback their tiles
                rendered as an empty tinted square, which reads as a broken
                image rather than a designed empty state. The band's ghosted
                ARTWORK stays absent for those sections, because that is a
                field ornament and "where no icon matches, use none" still
                holds there; this is a 92px tile that has to look like
                something. -#}
            <span class="mc-shot mc-shot--none" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#i-{{ ornament | default('ramen-bowl') }}"></use></svg></span>
            {%- endif %}
            <div class="mc-plate__text">
              <p class="mc-plate__head">
                <span class="mc-plate__name">{{ dish.name }}
                  {%- for flag in menuConcepts.legend %}
                    {%- if flag.flag in dish.dietary %}
                  <span class="mc-mark mc-mark--{{ flag.flag }}">
                    <span class="u-visually-hidden">{{ flag.label }}</span>
                    <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#{{ flag.icon }}"></use></svg>
                  </span>
                    {%- endif %}
                  {%- endfor %}
                </span>
                {%- if showPrices %}<span class="mc-plate__price">{{ dish.price }}</span>{% endif %}
              </p>
              {%- if dish.description %}
              <p class="mc-plate__desc">{{ dish.description }}</p>
              {%- endif %}
            </div>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- else %}
        <ul class="mc-lines">
          {%- for dish in rows %}
          <li class="mc-line">
            <span class="mc-line__name">{{ dish.name }}
              {%- for flag in menuConcepts.legend %}
                {%- if flag.flag in dish.dietary %}
              <span class="mc-mark mc-mark--{{ flag.flag }}">
                <span class="u-visually-hidden">{{ flag.label }}</span>
                <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#{{ flag.icon }}"></use></svg>
              </span>
                {%- endif %}
              {%- endfor %}
            </span>
            {%- if showPrices %}<span class="mc-line__price">{{ dish.price }}</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if dish.description %}
            <span class="mc-line__note">{{ dish.description }}</span>
            {%- endif %}
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- if variant == "b1" and featured %}
        {#- The preview pane, the reference's peek card. Sticky beside the
            list on wide viewports. A section with no photograph carrying
            reviewed alt renders no pane at all. -#}
        <aside class="mc-peek" aria-label="{{ section.label }}, featured dish">
          <img class="mc-peek__media"
            src="{{ featured.photo.src }}"
            alt="{{ featured.photo.alt }}"
            loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            width="{{ featured.photo.width }}" height="{{ featured.photo.height }}">
          <div class="mc-peek__body">
            <p class="mc-peek__eyebrow">Featured</p>
            <p class="mc-peek__name">{{ featured.dish.name }}</p>
            {%- if showPrices %}<p class="mc-peek__price">{{ featured.dish.price }}</p>{% endif %}
            {%- if featured.dish.description %}
            <p class="mc-peek__desc">{{ featured.dish.description }}</p>
            {%- endif %}
            <p class="mc-peek__where">Photographed at Convoy</p>
          </div>
        </aside>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{%- if mcChromeOn %}
<footer class="mc-foot">
  <h2 class="u-visually-hidden">Menu marks and allergen information</h2>
  <ul class="mc-notes">
    {%- for flag in menuConcepts.legend %}
    <li class="mc-notes__item">
      <span class="mc-mark mc-mark--{{ flag.flag }}" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#{{ flag.icon }}"></use></svg></span>
      <span><b>{{ flag.label }}.</b> {{ flag.note }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>

  {#- Named rather than guessed at. menu.json has no field for three of the
      legend above, computed from the rows this page renders. -#}
  {%- set unused = mcBands | unusedFlags(menuConcepts.legend) %}
  {%- if unused | length %}
  <p class="mc-foot__gap">
    Marked from data only. {{ unused | join(" and ") }} have no field on any dish yet,
    so nothing on this page carries {% if unused | length > 1 %}those marks{% else %}that mark{% endif %}.
  </p>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if variant == "a2" %}
  {#- One line rather than a caption on each of eleven tiles. Every dish
      photograph in the manifest was shot at Convoy, and an East Village menu
      showing them should say so once. -#}
  <p class="mc-foot__gap">Dish photography was shot at Convoy.</p>
  {%- endif %}

  <div class="mc-foot__fine">
    {%- for line in menuConcepts.footer %}
    <p>{{ line }}</p>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</footer>
{%- else %}
{#- Inside a location page the legend is the only part of the footer that
    belongs: the allergen fine print already lives in the page's FAQ, and
    repeating it under every room's menu would be three copies of the same
    sentence on one screen. -#}
<footer class="mc-foot mc-foot--inline">
  <h3 class="u-visually-hidden">Menu marks</h3>
  <ul class="mc-notes">
    {%- for flag in menuConcepts.legend %}
    <li class="mc-notes__item">
      <span class="mc-mark mc-mark--{{ flag.flag }}" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#{{ flag.icon }}"></use></svg></span>
      <span><b>{{ flag.label }}.</b> {{ flag.note }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- set unusedInline = mcBands | unusedFlags(menuConcepts.legend) %}
  <p class="mc-foot__gap">
    {%- if unusedInline | length %}
    Marked from data only. {{ unusedInline | join(" and ") }} have no field on any dish yet.
    {%- endif %}
    <a class="sect__link" href="/menu/">Compare the other rooms</a>.
  </p>
</footer>
{%- endif %}
